{"book":5,"chapter":27,"context":{"chapter":27,"title":"Stones, Altar and Twelve Curses","summary":"Once across the Jordan, Israel is to set up plastered stones inscribed with the law on Mount Ebal and build an altar there. Six tribes stand on Gerizim and six on Ebal while the Levites call out twelve curses, each answered 'Amen.'","background":"The valley between Gerizim and Ebal near Shechem forms a natural amphitheater. Writing in ink on plastered walls is known from the region, most famously a text about Balaam found at Deir Alla in Jordan. Joshua carries out this ceremony in Joshua 8:30-35, and Paul quotes verse 26 in Galatians 3:10.","customs":[{"term":"Amen","verses":"27:15-26","note":"A Hebrew word meaning 'surely' or 'so be it.' By saying it, the people bound themselves publicly to each statement."},{"term":"Whole stones","verses":"27:5-6","note":"The altar was to be built of uncut field stones, with no iron tool used on them, as in Exodus 20:25."}],"watchFor":["Many of the curses target sins done in secret (vv. 15, 24).","The list ends with a curse on not keeping 'all the words of this law' (v. 26)."],"connections":["Exodus 20:25","Joshua 8:30-35","Galatians 3:10","John 4:20"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְצַו","vaytzav","H6680","Hc/Vpw3ms","and he commanded"],["מֹשֶׁה","mosheh","H4872","HNpm","Moses"],["וְזִקְנֵי","veziknei","H2205","HC/Aampc","and [the] elders of"],["יִשְׂרָאֵל","yisra'el","H3478","HNpl","Israel"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["הָעָם","ha'am","H5971","HTd/Ncmsa","the people"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"],["שָׁמֹר","shamor","H8104","HVqaa","keep"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["כָּל","kol-","H3605","HNcmsc","all"],["הַמִּצְוָה","hamitzvah","H4687","HTd/Ncfsa","the commandment"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["אָנֹכִי","'anokhi","H595","HPp1bs","I"],["מְצַוֶּה","metzaveh","H6680","HVprmsa","[am] commanding"],["אֶתְכֶם","'etkhem","H853","HTo/Sp2mp","<obj.> you"],["הַיּוֹם","haiyom","H3117","HTd/Nc